# =============================================================================
# .gitignore — batch-delivery / EWGT 2026 paper repository
# =============================================================================
# Strategy: track code, small reference artifacts, paper-figure outputs.
# Ignore everything that can be regenerated from code + data, and everything
# that is bulk data. Large reproducible artifacts are fetched via the data
# download script (see docs/REPRODUCING_PAPER.md).
# =============================================================================

# ─── Python ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
.venv/
venv/
env/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
build/
dist/
pip-wheel-metadata/

# ─── Bulk inputs (fetched via scripts/data/download_inputs.py) ───────────────
# HAGRID demand shapefiles, PLZ geodata, hub CSVs are ~400 MB.
# See docs/REPRODUCING_PAPER.md for the canonical download source.
data/*
!data/README.md
!data/MANIFEST.md

# ─── Bulk outputs (regenerable via the pipeline) ─────────────────────────────
# Default-ignore everything under results/, then explicitly un-ignore the
# canonical and supplementary paper outputs. The _archive/ tree stays
# gitignored — it is preserved locally for review provenance but not shipped.
# Bulk binary patterns (*.pkl, *.parquet, *.npz) further down still apply
# inside the un-ignored paths.
results/*
!results/README.md
!results/CANONICAL.md
!results/paper_ewgt_2026/
!results/paper_ewgt_2026/**
!results/paper_outputs_2026_05_30/
!results/paper_outputs_2026_05_30/**
!results/paper_results_2026_05_30/
!results/paper_results_2026_05_30/**
!results/runs/
!results/runs/**
!results/supplementary/
!results/supplementary/**

# Large binary artifacts that can always be regenerated
*.pkl
*.pickle
*.joblib
*.parquet
*.feather
*.npz
*.npy
*.h5
*.hdf5

# Large geospatial binaries (shapefile bundles, tiles)
*.shp
*.shx
*.dbf
*.prj
*.cpg
*.sbn
*.sbx
*.osm.pbf
*.osm
*.mbtiles

# Compressed archives — track sources, not bundles
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
*.zip
*.7z
*.rar

# Elevation tiles
*.hgt

# ─── Routing service runtime ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
valhalla/custom_files/*
!valhalla/custom_files/.gitkeep
vroom/*.json
vroom/access.log

# ─── Hash registry (regenerated on demand) ───────────────────────────────────
.file_hashes.txt

# ─── Frozen legacy snapshot (already preserved offline) ──────────────────────
archive/

# ─── Local agent / IDE state (not for upstream) ──────────────────────────────
.claude/
memory/
.vscode/
.idea/
.cursor/
.aider*
.windsurf/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ─── AI-agent session artefacts (ephemeral, not shared knowledge) ────────────
# Plans/specs written by agents during a session live here; they are not
# project documentation. CLAUDE.md / AGENTS.md / GEMINI.md ARE tracked
# (shared repo instructions) — only the per-session output is ignored.
docs/superpowers/
docs/codebase/
docs/_paper_patches_*.md

# ─── Generic runtime ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
outputs/
logs/
tmp/
*.log
!vroom/access.log.example

# ─── Notebook checkpoints ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.ipynb_checkpoints/
*-checkpoint.ipynb
